      "content_html": "<img src=\"http://static.dezeen.com/uploads/2026/09/monastic-field-roomoor-india_dezeen_2364_sq_0-411x411.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p>Architecture studio Roomoor has completed Monastic Field, a concrete home within a temple precinct in Baleshwar that recalls the rock-cut monk's dwellings of the Deccan Plateau. Set within the site of a Jain temple, the homes was designed for the family that originally donated the land for the temple in 2005. As the temple site</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com/2026/10/11/monastic-field-roomoor-india/\">\"Monolithic\" concrete house informed by rock-cut monastic homes</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com\">Dezeen</a>.</p>",
