    {
      "id": "https://www.archdaily.com/1186200/designing-the-in-between-from-tactical-interventions-to-urban-policy-in-barcelona",
      "url": "https://www.archdaily.com/1186200/designing-the-in-between-from-tactical-interventions-to-urban-policy-in-barcelona",
      "title": "[ArchDaily] Designing the In-Between: From Tactical Interventions to Urban Policy in Barcelona",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://images.adsttc.com/media/images/6abe/c691/27ac/8d01/89cb/af23/large_jpg/designing-the-in-between-from-tactical-interventions-to-urban-policy-in-barcelona_1.jpg?1790887573\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p>In <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/europe\">Europe</a>, cities are confronting the challenge of <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/1010388/what-is-an-urban-oasis-combating-the-excessive-heat-of-cities?ad_source=search&amp;ad_medium=search_result_articles\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">adapting existing urban conditions to a changing climate and warming summers</a> while <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/1035817/designing-for-tomorrow-nature-positive-solutions-in-urban-environments?ad_source=search&amp;ad_medium=search_result_articles\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">improving access to nature, quality public spaces, and the resources of everyday routines.</a> <a href=\"https://regreeneration.eu/?utm_medium=website&amp;utm_source=archdaily.com\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">ReGreeneration</a>, a Horizon Europe initiative working across nine European cities, approaches <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/1035869/bugs-bees-and-trees-how-to-integrate-biodiversity-in-the-built-environment?ad_source=search&amp;ad_medium=search_result_articles\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">this challenge through urban renaturing at the neighborhood scale</a>. Combining strategies for <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/1042276/paris-as-a-living-laboratory-proximity-inclusion-and-the-school-as-climate-and-social-infrastructure?ad_campaign=normal-tag\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">complete neighborhoods, communal spaces, and nature-based solutions for cities</a>, the <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/barcelona\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona </a>project examines how climate adaptation is embedded within residual, peripheral spaces of daily life. As part of a series following <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/tag/regreeneration\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">ReGreeneration</a> across the <a href=\"https://www.archdaily.com/1040595/reimagining-the-complete-neighborhood-through-urban-renaturing?ad_source=search&amp;ad_medium=projects_tab&amp;ad_source=search&amp;ad_medium=search_result_all?ad_medium=widget&amp;ad_name=related-article&amp;ad_content=1042276\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">participating cities, this article turns to Barcelona, where the project is working in the Trinitat Nova neighborhood</a> to explore how <a href=\"https://regreeneration.eu/cities/barcelona/?utm_medium=website&amp;utm_source=archdaily.com\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">small, often overlooked, urban spaces contribute to broader models of regeneration.</a></p>",
      "date_published": "2026-10-11T07:30:00+00:00",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "ArchDaily",
          "url": "https://www.archdaily.com"
        }
      ],
      "image": "https://images.adsttc.com/media/images/6abe/c691/27ac/8d01/89cb/af23/large_jpg/designing-the-in-between-from-tactical-interventions-to-urban-policy-in-barcelona_1.jpg?1790887573",
      "_score": 47,
      "_quality": 72,
      "_relevance": 55,
      "_local_score": 0,
      "_content_type": "analysis"
    },
    {
      "id": "https://www.archdaily.com/1186616/resonance-tallinn-architecture-biennale-installation-aru-ma-architects",
      "url": "https://www.archdaily.com/1186616/resonance-tallinn-architecture-biennale-installation-aru-ma-architects",
      "title": "[ArchDaily] RESONANCE - Tallinn Architecture Biennale Installation / Aru Ma- Architects",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://images.adsttc.com/media/images/6ac8/ace4/b2c4/c300/0178/e4c4/large_jpg/IMG_9828.jpg?1791536587\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p>Set against Tallinn's rapidly commercializing urban backdrop, the installation offers a sheltered courtyard detached from its surroundings, creating a deliberate pause. Here, the sea breeze whispers against silent stones, and sunlight filters onto the warm, sweeping curves of plywood screens. It is a spatial privilege carved from ordinary materials, filtering out external chaos for pure atmospheric luxury.</p>",
