      "title": "[Canadian Architect] New SEAandSKY pedestrian bridge opens connection to downtown Squamish",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=www.canadianarchitect.com&amp;sz=128\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\nSet within the traditional territory of the Sḵwx̱ wú7mesh Úxwumixw, the SEAandSKY Pedestrian Bridge—British Columbia’s first operable pedestrian drawbridge—has opened across the Mamquam Blind Channel. The bridge links Bosa Properties’ SEAandSKY waterfront development to downtown Squamish. Vancouver-based architecture firm RSAAW, named one of Canadian Architect and Twenty + Change’s emerging talents in 2024, shaped the…",
