      "url": "https://www.dezeen.com/2026/10/07/ekarth-studio-maestro-ilaiyaraaja-centre/",
      "title": "[Dezeen] Sculptural music centre shows bamboo as \"a serious construction material\"",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"http://static.dezeen.com/uploads/2026/10/maestro-ilaiyaraaja-centre-music-learning-research-ekarth-studio-architecture-education-universities-bamboo-india-chennai_dezeen_2364_sq2-411x411.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🎨 🌲 🏔️ 🔭 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.dezeen.com%2F2026%2F10%2F07%2Fekarth-studio-maestro-ilaiyaraaja-centre%2F\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\n<p>Dramatic bamboo vaults form a series of teaching and research spaces at Maestro Ilaiyaraaja Centre for Music Learning and Research, completed by Indian studio Ekarth Studio in the state of Tamil Nadu. Located on the 250-hectare IIT Madras university campus in Chennai, the centre comprises a series of bamboo pavilions used by student musicians, engineers</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com/2026/10/07/ekarth-studio-maestro-ilaiyaraaja-centre/\">Sculptural music centre shows bamboo as \"a serious construction material\"</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com\">Dezeen</a>.</p>",
